{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest effect observed so far is the multiprofile boost for scvi_n200 (0.520 single → 0.650/0.653 multi, ~+13 pts), while singleprofile RNA encoders rank scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 > scgpt. Image-only (resnet50) is essentially at chance (0.208). Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the multiprofile gain is a general property of seeing multiple profiles or is specific to scvi's learned latent representation. Question: config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) directly tests this by changing only the profile setting from config_001 (pca, single: 0.485). If pca also jumps substantially, multiprofile is a universal design lever; if it stays near 0.485, the gain is tied to scvi's learned representation. This is the best next experiment because it isolates one variable (profile setting) against an already-completed baseline, reduces uncertainty about a core architectural decision before committing budget to multimodal or additional encoder combinations, and the aggregation choice (avgpool) is already shown to be near-equivalent to transformer, so it does not confound the comparison."
}

